Conclusion

By default Selenium attempts to open a real browser when a WebDriver is created, but in a Jenkins pipeline you normally run browsers in headless mode, use a virtual display, or run browsers on remote nodes so no visible window appears on the Jenkins host. Choose headless for CI stability and resource savings; pick Xvfb or remote Grid only when you need a visual session for debugging or special functionality.

