Notes, troubleshooting, and improvements

If using a plain python image, you must install Chrome and chromedriver (or use webdriver-manager as above) and ensure /dev/shm is large enough or add --disable-dev-shm-usage.

If a test needs a visible UI for debugging, run the same Docker image but remove headless flag or use VNC from selenium/standalone-chrome to view the session; otherwise CI runs should be headless for stability.

For flaky tests, consider using Xvfb or Selenium Grid (remote nodes) to scale browsers off the Jenkins controller.

If you prefer pytest-selenium plugin, you can override its chrome options in conftest.py or pass plugin CLI options; the principle (add headless flags) is the same.

